.\" Title: vrc-keys
.\" Author: vrc contributors
.\" Manual section: 1
.\"
.TH VRC\-KEYS 1 "2025" "vrc" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
vrc\-keys \- send keystrokes to a running command inside a vrc instance

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vrc
\fBkeys\fR \fIPID\fR [\fB\-c\fR \fICOMMAND\fR] \fIKEYS\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
Send keystrokes to the virtual terminal (VTTY) of a command running inside a vrc instance. The keys are injected into the command's input buffer as if they had been typed at the keyboard, allowing interaction with commands that are detached from any terminal.

Connects to the target instance's UDS control socket at \fB~/.local/share/vrc/control\-{pid}.sock\fR and sends the key input request.

This is particularly useful for sending signals or input to background or detached commands, such as interrupting a long-running process with \fBCtrl\-C\fR, answering a prompt, or typing text into an interactive program.

Keystrokes are specified as a string. Special keys use the following format:

.TS
l l.
ctrl-c	Ctrl + C (SIGINT)
ctrl-d	Ctrl + D (EOF)
ctrl-z	Ctrl + Z (SIGTSTP)
enter	Newline / carriage return
tab	Tab character
escape	Escape character
up	Up arrow
down	Down arrow
left	Left arrow
right	Right arrow
.TE

Literal text (e.g., \fBhello world\fR) is sent as-is. Multiple keystrokes can be combined by separating them with spaces (e.g., \fBctrl-c enter\fR sends Ctrl\-C followed by Enter).

.SH ARGUMENTS

.TP
.B PID
OS process ID of the target vrc instance.

.TP
.B KEYS
Keystrokes to send (required). See the DESCRIPTION section above for the list of supported key names and formats.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-command " " \fICOMMAND\fR
ID of the target command (omit for the first/only command).

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information and exit.

.SH EXAMPLES

.PP
Send Ctrl\-C to interrupt the only command in an instance:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc keys 12345 ctrl-c\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Send Ctrl\-C to a specific command by ID:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc keys 12345 \-c cmd_abc ctrl-c\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Type text into a command's terminal:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc keys 12345 "hello world"\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Send Ctrl\-C followed by Enter:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc keys 12345 ctrl-c enter\fR
.fi
.RE

.PP
Answer a yes/no prompt in a running command:
.RS
.PP
.nf
\fB$ vrc keys 12345 \-c cmd_abc y enter\fR
.fi
.RE

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Keystrokes sent successfully.

.TP
.B 1
Error (instance not found, command not found, connection failed, etc.).

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vrc (1),
.BR vrc\-list (1),
.BR vrc\-cat (1),
.BR vrc\-spawn\-in (1)
